- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests`

**How to implement.** The experiment file records the exclusions of its data's points and the corrections of its setup, each with its reason or audit note (001 §K 'Raw data is immutable; exclusions carry a reason and stay visible in plots, marked'; 001 §K 'Corrections: re-point an experiment's setup after the fact (e.g. "LR was at −45"), with a mandatory audit note'; 001 §E 'Lab files are read-only for the app. Exclusions, corrections and mappings live in the experiment file'; the S9.3 brief; the S9.2 mapper's request: `MappedRow` carries no row number, so an exclusion numbers its point). This is one step because the two records' new fields change every consumer at once (the step 261 precedent); the messages that set them are steps 315 and 316. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, directly before `MappedAttachment` (step 291): (a) `MappedPointNumber of int` with `.value`, a point's 1-based place among the points its attachment's row selection keeps, in file order (the answer of `ExperimentDataProxy.readMapped`, step 305): `static member tryCreate (number : int) : MappedPointNumber option` answers `None` below 1. (b) `ExclusionReason of string` with `.value`: `static member tryCreate (text : string) : ExclusionReason option` keeps the text as given and answers `None` for an empty or white-space text. (c) `PointExclusion = { point : MappedPointNumber; reason : ExclusionReason }`. No int tag is added: none of them is a closed set. (2) `MappedAttachment` gains `exclusions : PointExclusion list` after `rows`: its exclusions in point order, at most one per point. An exclusion belongs to the mapped attachment because it numbers that attachment's points: attaching a file anew builds a new mapped attachment, which starts with none. On `MappedAttachment`: `member this.withExclusion (exclusion : PointExclusion) : MappedAttachment` (that point's exclusion replaced, or the new one inserted in point order), `member this.withoutExclusion (point : MappedPointNumber) : MappedAttachment` (that point's exclusion removed; the attachment unchanged when it has none) and `member this.tryFindExclusion (point : MappedPointNumber) : PointExclusion option`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`, after `ExperimentNotes` (step 285): `CorrectionNote of string` with `.value` and `static member tryCreate (text : string) : CorrectionNote option` (`None` for an empty or white-space text); `SetupCorrection = { previous : SetupReference; corrected : SetupReference; note : CorrectionNote }`, one re-pointing of the experiment's setup and why it was made. `Experiment` gains `corrections : SetupCorrection list` after `dataOpt`, oldest first. `commit` (step 290) gives an appended experiment `[]` and keeps an edited one's, so an edit never loses its audit trail. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/experiment.schema.json` (steps 288, 290, 291), schema version 1 kept (no kit of the old shape exists outside test output, .spec-md §7): a non-null `dataOpt` holds exactly `attachment`, `profile`, `rows` and `exclusions`, an array of objects holding exactly `point` (an integer from 1) and `reason` (a string holding a non-white-space character); `experiment` also holds `corrections`, an array of objects holding exactly `previous` and `corrected` (each the object `experiment.setup` is, step 261) and `note` (a string holding a non-white-space character). `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs`: `copyExperimentsFrom` (steps 224, 261, 291, 306) keeps each copied experiment's exclusions and corrections as written; only its id, its name and its attachment's path are given anew, as before. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: the `AttachDataFile` arm (step 310) builds its mapped attachment with `exclusions = []`; nothing else in the window changes. (6) Every fixture that builds a `MappedAttachment` sets `exclusions = []`, and every fixture that builds an `Experiment` sets `corrections = []`, every fact keeping its assertions: in `ExperimentProxyTests`, `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests`, `KitContentFileJsonTests`, `KitLibraryTests`, `ExperimentCopyTests`, `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests`, `SetupTests`, `SetupModelTests`, `KitWindowModelTests`, `ExperimentDataProxyTests`, `ExperimentDataStoreTests`, `ExperimentModelTests`, `SolverHandoffWindowTests`, `ScrollExtentTests`, `InverseConstructorTests` and `KitWindowTests`, whichever of them build one. No other field, member or option is added. Tests. `KitTests` (step 122) gains `a point exclusion needs a point from 1 and a reason, and an attachment keeps one exclusion per point in point order`: `MappedPointNumber.tryCreate` of 1 and 7 keeps them and of 0 and −1 answers `None`; `ExclusionReason.tryCreate "cosmic ray"` keeps the text and `""` and `"  "` answer `None`; a test-local mapped attachment with no exclusion, `withExclusion` of point 3 (`cosmic ray`) then of point 1 (`shutter`) holds points 1 and 3 in that order; `withExclusion` of point 3 with `stray light` replaces its reason and keeps two exclusions; `tryFindExclusion` of 3 answers it and of 2 `None`; `withoutExclusion` of 1 leaves point 3 alone, and of 2 the attachment unchanged. `ExperimentProxyTests` gains `a correction note refuses a blank text, and a committed experiment starts with no correction and keeps its corrections through an edit`: `CorrectionNote.tryCreate "LR was at -45"` keeps the text and `"  "` answers `None`; `commit` of a target over `Bench` revision 1 appends an experiment with `corrections = []`; that experiment given one test-local correction (`Bench` revision 1 → `Plate` revision 1, `LR was at -45`) through a `with` copy and stored back (`withStoredExperiment`, step 294), then `edit` and `commit` of a target over `Bench` revision 1 keep the correction. `KitContentFileJsonTests` (steps 146, 261, 288, 291): `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text` also round-trips E1 whose data excludes point 3 for `cosmic ray` and whose corrections hold `CPL-(LR#45)-CPL` revision 1 → `CPL-(LR#-45)-CPL` revision 1 with the note `LR was at -45`; `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds` also refuses an exclusion of point 0, an exclusion whose reason is `"  "`, a `dataOpt` without `exclusions`, an experiment without `corrections` and a correction without `note`. `ExperimentCopyTests` (step 291): `a copy keeps each copied experiment's import profile and row selection` also finds the copied experiment's exclusion of point 2 (`saturated`) and its one correction as written.

**Acceptance.** After the two records gain their fields, a mapped attachment MUST hold its point exclusions (a point from 1 and a non-blank reason, one per point, in point order) and an experiment its setup corrections (previous, corrected and a non-blank note, oldest first), the experiment file MUST round-trip both and refuse a malformed one, a commit MUST start an experiment with no correction and an edit keep them, and a copy MUST keep both; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a point exclusion needs a point from 1 and a reason, and an attachment keeps one exclusion per point in point order` and `a correction note refuses a blank text, and a committed experiment starts with no correction and keeps its corrections through an edit`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds` and `a copy keeps each copied experiment's import profile and row selection`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.
